LEVEL3 {}

 AUTO VALIDATOR - SECURITY AND ACCOUNTING

 These are INSTALL DEFAULTS.  The first time Auto Validator starts it
 copies these values into its settings file (HVSAVSET.DAT).  After that,
 change settings ONLINE from the Auto Validator sysop menu (Settings) -
 changes made there take effect immediately, without a restart.  To
 re-apply the values below, use "Reset settings to defaults" in that
 menu.

 This is the key a user must have to request validation.  If it is
 empty, anyone may request validation, subject to the normal checks.

 Default: (none)

VALIDKEY {} S 15 Key a user needs to request validation

 The key needed to use the Auto Validator sysop menu and the sysop
 global commands.  Users with this key are never validated themselves;
 they manage the validator instead.  WARNING: users with this key can
 validate and devalidate other users, so give it to sysops only.

 Default: SYSOP

CNFGACES {SYSOP} S 15 Key needed for the sysop menu and commands

 The validation method (1-5) applied when a user enters the correct
 code from their validation email.  Methods 1-5 are defined by the
 MTDnCLS, MTDnKEY, MTDnCRED and MTDnPAYM settings below.

 Default: 1

EMAILMTD {Validation method for email validations: 1} N 1 5

 The maximum number of VALIDATED users that may share one email
 address.  Once this many validated users use an address, no further
 user may be validated with it.

 Default: 1

MAXEMAIL {Max validated users per email address: 1} N 1 100

 The class a user is switched to when validated with method 1.  Leave
 empty for no class change.  The class must exist in your Accounts
 setup; if it does not, the class change is skipped and a warning is
 written to the Audit Trail.

 Default: (none)

MTD1CLS {} S 15 New class for method 1 validation

 A key given to users validated with method 1.  Leave empty to give
 no key.

 Default: (none)

MTD1KEY {} S 15 New key for method 1 validation

 Credits posted to a user validated with method 1.  Zero posts none.

 Default: 0

MTD1CRED {Credits posted for method 1 validations: 0} L 0 1000000

 Whether method 1 credits are posted as FREE or PAID (for system
 accounting).

 Default: FREE

MTD1PAYM {Credit type for method 1 validations: FREE} E FREE PAID

 The class a user is switched to when validated with method 2.  Leave
 empty for no class change.

 Default: (none)

MTD2CLS {} S 15 New class for method 2 validation

 A key given to users validated with method 2.

 Default: (none)

MTD2KEY {} S 15 New key for method 2 validation

 Credits posted to a user validated with method 2.

 Default: 0

MTD2CRED {Credits posted for method 2 validations: 0} L 0 1000000

 Whether method 2 credits are posted as FREE or PAID.

 Default: FREE

MTD2PAYM {Credit type for method 2 validations: FREE} E FREE PAID

 The class a user is switched to when validated with method 3.  Leave
 empty for no class change.

 Default: (none)

MTD3CLS {} S 15 New class for method 3 validation

 A key given to users validated with method 3.

 Default: (none)

MTD3KEY {} S 15 New key for method 3 validation

 Credits posted to a user validated with method 3.

 Default: 0

MTD3CRED {Credits posted for method 3 validations: 0} L 0 1000000

 Whether method 3 credits are posted as FREE or PAID.

 Default: FREE

MTD3PAYM {Credit type for method 3 validations: FREE} E FREE PAID

 The class a user is switched to when validated with method 4.  Leave
 empty for no class change.

 Default: (none)

MTD4CLS {} S 15 New class for method 4 validation

 A key given to users validated with method 4.

 Default: (none)

MTD4KEY {} S 15 New key for method 4 validation

 Credits posted to a user validated with method 4.

 Default: 0

MTD4CRED {Credits posted for method 4 validations: 0} L 0 1000000

 Whether method 4 credits are posted as FREE or PAID.

 Default: FREE

MTD4PAYM {Credit type for method 4 validations: FREE} E FREE PAID

