LEVEL4 {}

 AUTO VALIDATOR - GENERAL CONFIGURATION

 These are INSTALL DEFAULTS (see the note at the top of the Level 3
 options).  Once the module has run, change them online from the Auto
 Validator sysop menu.

 If YES, users who have the validation key but are not yet validated
 are asked at logon whether they want to validate now.

 Default: NO

AVATLOGN {Offer validation to users at logon: NO} B

 The first character of the Auto Validator sysop global commands (for
 example @V, @L).  It must not clash with any other global command
 trigger on your system.

 Default: @

AVGLOB {Global command trigger character: @} C

 How email is described to users in Auto Validator messages, for
 example "Internet".

 Default: Internet

EMAILTYP {Internet} S 20 Type of email address (shown to users)

 The address prefix that routes a message out through your Internet
 mail gateway.  The validation email is addressed to this prefix
 followed by the user's address.

 Default: IN:

EMAILPFX {IN:} S 5 Internet email address prefix

 An email domain that may not be used for validation - typically your
 own BBS's domain, so users cannot validate with a mailbox on your own
 system.  Leave empty to allow all domains.  For a longer list, put
 one entry per line in HVSAVBAD.TXT in the BBS directory; any address
 containing one of those entries is refused.

 Default: (none)

BADEMAIL {} S 37 Email domain refused for validation

 The number of times a user may fail validation (three wrong codes in
 one visit counts as one failure).  After that the sysop must reset
 them with the devalidate (@D) or override (@O) global command.  Zero
 means no limit.

 Default: 3

MAXATMPT {Failed validations allowed per user: 3} N 0 100

 The Auto Validator activity log, a text file in the BBS directory.
 Every validation, failure and sysop action is logged with the date
 and time.  Leave empty to disable logging.

 Default: HVSAV.LOG

LOGFILE {HVSAV.LOG} S 40 Auto Validator activity log file

